imud (1.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Sea state: significant wave height, wave period, roll/pitch periods and
    significant amplitudes from the heave/attitude oscillations ([fusion]
    wave_tau_s, WAVE_VALID flag). Compass-health diagnostics (mag_anomaly,
    mag_residual) computed in the filter. ENGINE_ON flag exports the
    engine-vibration detector.
  * Binary stream packet v14 (260 bytes; fields appended before the CRC).
    Wire-pinned consumers must be rebuilt together with the daemon; libimud
    applications are unaffected.
  * imud_client.h is deprecated (use libimud) and no longer installed.
  * Fix the CI verification steps added in 1.3 (hardening-check fortify
    false positive on libimud.so; versioned-symbol handling in the ABI
    surface check); CI now also covers arm64 and ASan/UBSan.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Sat, 11 Jul 2026 11:35:35 -0700

imud (1.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship libimud, an ABI-stable client shared library (own package: libimud),
    with imud.h, pkg-config metadata, and man 3 libimud. No wire change
    (packet stays v12).

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Fri, 10 Jul 2026 12:00:00 -0700

imud (1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Binary stream packet version 12 (228 bytes): add gyro bias (x/y/z) + variance,
    heave rate, and an accel-quiescence metric; add a HEAVE_VALID flag. Stream
    consumers (bridges, imud-mon, custom clients) must be rebuilt against the new
    packet layout.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Fri, 10 Jul 2026 03:00:00 -0700

imud (1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add optional bridge daemons, each its own package: imud-signalk,
    imud-mqtt, imud-influxdb, imud-mavlink.
  * Binary stream packet version 11: add heave and magnetic-declination fields.
  * Add heave estimator and a rough-sea fusion revision.
  * Add level-gated logging (debug/info/warn/error).
  * Ship GNU + Debian standard documentation; install per-package docs under
    /usr/share/doc/.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Fri, 10 Jul 2026 01:32:55 -0700

imud (1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: quaternion MEKF attitude/heading from an I²C IMU +
    magnetometer; NMEA 0183, high-rate binary UDP, and a local AF_UNIX
    subscription stream; World Magnetic Model true heading; gyro/accel/mag
    calibration (imud-cal); status and monitoring (imud-status, imud-mon);
    a hardened systemd service.

 -- Richard Simpson <richcreations@gmail.com>  Mon, 06 Jul 2026 12:00:00 -0700
